    <h2>What Is the Strawberry Cheesequake Blizzard?</h2>
  <p>The Strawberry Cheesequake Blizzard combines real cheesecake pieces with sweet strawberry topping and crumbly pie crust, all blended into DQ vanilla soft serve. It is richer and more complex than a simple strawberry Blizzard — the cheesecake pieces add a dense, creamy layer that elevates the fruit flavor. Find this and all Blizzard flavors on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a> or the <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats page</a>.</p>

  <h2>Cheesequake vs. Royal New York Cheesecake Blizzard</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>What Sets It Apart</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Strawberry Cheesequake Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>~520</td><td>Cheesecake + strawberry + pie crust</td></tr><tr><td>Royal New York Cheesecake Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>~510</td><td>Graham cracker + cheesecake + strawberry center</td></tr><tr><td>Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>540</td><td>Summer seasonal — fudge swirl added</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

  <h2>Three Reasons to Order the Strawberry Cheesequake</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Layered flavor complexity</strong> — Cheesecake + strawberry + pie crust is more interesting per spoonful than a single candy-bar Blizzard</li>
    <li><strong>Lighter than chocolate Blizzards</strong> — At ~520 cal Small it is below the calorie count of <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's</a> (600) or <a href="/items/turtle-pecan-blizzard">Turtle Pecan Cluster</a> (570)</li>
    <li><strong>Pairs well after savory food</strong> — The fruity strawberry notes work as a natural palate cleanser after a burger or chicken basket</li>
  </ul>

