<h2>Strawberry Cheesequake — Full Ordering Guide</h2>
<p>A few ordering tips to get the most from the Strawberry Cheesequake Blizzard at your next <a href="/locations">DQ visit</a>:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Order a Mini first ($3.99)</strong> — The Cheesequake is one of the more flavor-forward Blizzards. A Mini is the right amount for a first taste before committing to a Medium or Large.</li>
<li><strong>Request extra strawberry topping</strong> — If you want the fruit flavor more prominent, ask for an extra pour of strawberry topping (~$0.50 upcharge at most locations).</li>
<li><strong>Lighter blend</strong> — Requesting a lighter blend keeps the cheesecake pieces in larger, denser chunks rather than partially dissolved — a noticeably different texture experience.</li>
<li><strong>Pair with a lighter entrée</strong> — At ~520 cal Small, the Cheesequake is a medium-calorie Blizzard. It pairs well after an <a href="/items/original-cheeseburger">Original Cheeseburger</a> (400 cal) or <a href="/items/grilled-chicken-sandwich">Grilled Chicken Sandwich</a> (390 cal) without pushing the total meal into very high calorie territory.</li>
</ul>
